notes:
The second-spell trigger is the ONLY blocker, and it is the same capability the `esper_sentinel` gap record already names -- closing `per-player-spell-ordinal` closes both cards. The other two printed lines are expressible with today's vocabulary and are written out below; the attack trigger was verified against the shipped `frontier_warmonger` and `combat_calligrapher` answers, which both use `creatures_attack_player` with the `attackers` binding, and against `combat.finish_attackers`, which fires that event once per defending seat with `attackers` set to the subset declared against *that* defender (and records the defender as the defending PLAYER even for an attack aimed at a planeswalker they control -- so `defending: "you"` covers "you and/or planeswalkers you control" exactly, with nothing extra needed). `{"count": {"binding": "attackers"}}` is a legal value: `values.evaluate_value` sends `count` through `resolve_pool`, and a bare `{"binding": ...}` selector returns the seeded oids without a zone default. Drop the third ability in the moment `nth` works on `spell_cast`:

{
  "card": {
    "id": "mangara_the_diplomat",
    "name": "Mangara, the Diplomat",
    "oracle_text": "Lifelink\nWhenever an opponent attacks with creatures, if two or more of those creatures are attacking you and/or planeswalkers you control, draw a card.\nWhenever an opponent casts their second spell each turn, draw a card.",
    "mana_cost": "{3}{W}",
    "types": ["Creature"],
    "supertypes": ["Legendary"],
    "subtypes": ["Human", "Cleric"],
    "power": 2,
    "toughness": 4,
    "colors": ["W"],
    "color_identity": ["W"],
    "keywords": ["lifelink"],
    "abilities": [
      {
        "kind": "triggered",
        "text": "Whenever an opponent attacks with creatures, if two or more of those creatures are attacking you and/or planeswalkers you control, draw a card.",
        "trigger": {
          "event": "creatures_attack_player",
          "controller": "opponent",
          "defending": "you",
          "condition": {
            "cmp": ">=",
            "left": {"count": {"binding": "attackers"}},
            "right": {"const": 2}
          }
        },
        "effects": [{"op": "draw", "amount": {"const": 1}}]
      },
      {
        "kind": "triggered",
        "text": "Whenever an opponent casts their second spell each turn, draw a card.",
        "trigger": {
          "event": "spell_cast",
          "controller": "opponent",
          "nth": 2
        },
        "effects": [{"op": "draw", "amount": {"const": 1}}]
      }
    ]
  },
  "expectation": {"zone": "battlefield", "battlefield_count": 33, "hand_size": {"0": 1}}
}

The expectation is the weak-fallback shape on purpose: the harness casts Mangara in your own precombat main and stops, so neither trigger can fire -- nothing attacks and nothing is cast afterwards -- and lifelink deals no damage. `battlefield_count` 33 is the 32 starting permanents plus Mangara; `hand_size` 1 is the spare Forest left behind.
